---
// sow-230: THE MEMBER-TIER INVITE LANDING. Audience-neutral on purpose: any campaign points at this one URL
// with its own ?coupon=, so a new invite audience needs a coupon and a link rather than a new page. That is
// why this replaced /linkedin-invite/ rather than sitting beside it.
//
// IT EXISTS BECAUSE THE PAGE BEFORE IT ADVERTISED CREATOR BENEFITS WHILE GRANTING THE MEMBER TIER. The tier
// label and price were correct (both come from tierDisplay), but the benefit PROSE was inherited from the
// Creator page it was copied from, so a $50 member invite promised publishing, syndication, a creator
// profile, weekly shop talk and the first-touch revenue program. The owner caught it. See the note above
// memberBenefits for why the fix is structural rather than editorial.
//
// SECTIONS DELETED RATHER THAN REWRITTEN: "why a network" (sells publishing), the four-way revenue splits
// (the Creator program; a Member earns through invites only), and the shop-talk band (a Creator benefit).
// Rewriting them means hand-writing benefit claims again, which is exactly what failed. A short honest page
// beats a long one with landmines.
//
// The SOW-119 mechanics under the skin, per the 2026-07-18 QA feedback: NO secret token links. A shared
// link carries a plain visible ?coupon=LINKEDINCONNECT, which prefills the chip (still editable, applied
// badge while it matches); with no param the chip is a hand-editable field (manual entry at signup).
// The CTA is the same Turnstile-gated /signup/start flow as /membership/, plus the coupon parameter.
// TITLE: pass the BARE title, with no brand suffix. BaseLayout builds `fullTitle` as `${title} | GBTI
// Network` and uses it for BOTH <title> and og:title, so a title that carries the brand itself double-brands
// the page. This one shipped as "Codeable experts: your first year on us · GBTI Network | GBTI Network" and
// was caught in a Slack unfurl of a real invite (owner, 2026-08-13), which is the worst place to find it:
// og:title is what every share preview shows.
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { REF_COOKIE, REF_VIA_COOKIE } from '../../lib/referral';
import { TOUCH_CAPTURE_ENABLED, TOUCH_SID_COOKIE } from '../../lib/touch.mjs';
import {
  BILLING_PERIOD,
  INVITE_PCT,
  TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY,
  SIGNUP_BASE,
} from '../../lib/membership';
import { tierDisplay } from '../../lib/tiers';

// sow-230: THIS INVITE CONFERS `member`, NOT `creator`, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE DIFFERENCE FROM THE PAGE THIS
// WAS COPIED FROM. The owner asked for "the $50/yr membership"; membership/tiers.mjs:17 records member as
// $5 monthly / $50 annual against creator at $15 / $150. `house/coupons.yml` names `tier: member` on
// LINKEDINCONNECT, and since aa22db3 that tier is stamped into the redemption record and written into the
// fold rather than re-derived, so the grant and this page agree only if BOTH say member.
//
// The failure mode this guards is a copy bug, not a config bug: the Codeable page calls its grant "the
// network's top tier", which is TRUE of creator and FALSE of member. Copying that sentence onto a member
// coupon advertises the wrong tier at the wrong price while granting the right one, which is worse than
// either mistake alone because the config looks correct.
//
// The constants are RENAMED rather than left as `creator`. `const creator = tierDisplay('member')` would
// work and would be a false name, which is the exact defect class this repo has been chasing all week.
// Bound to the single source of truth (house/membership-tiers.yml via tierDisplay) so the label and the
// "if you stay" price can never drift from it.
const memberTier = tierDisplay('member');
const TIER_LABEL = memberTier?.label ?? 'Network Member';
const TIER_PRICE_LABEL = `$${memberTier?.priceAnnual ?? 50}`;

// THE BENEFIT LIST IS RENDERED FROM house/membership-tiers.yml AND IS NOT WRITTEN HERE. That is the whole
// point of this file existing, and it is a correction rather than a style preference.
//
// The page this replaced (/linkedin-invite/) got the tier LABEL and the PRICE right, because both came from
// tierDisplay(). Its benefit PROSE was hand-written and stayed on the Creator page it was copied from, so a
// member-tier invite went live promising publishing, syndication, a creator profile, weekly shop talk and
// the first-touch revenue program. NONE of those are member benefits. The config was correct and only the
// sentences lied, which is the hardest version to catch: the checks that scanned for "Content Creator",
// "top tier" and "$150" all came back clean, because prose that promises publishing never names the tier.
//
// house/membership-tiers.yml states the rule about itself in its own header: "BENEFIT COPY IS A LEGAL LINE
// ON A PAID PAGE ... it must NEVER advertise a benefit that does not exist." So the fix is not better
// proofreading, it is removing the ability to type a benefit here at all. If a claim is not a bullet in
// that file, it cannot reach this page.
//
// Member, as of writing: post comments, full Discord, read members-only content and comment bodies, curate
// your feed. Revenue is the INVITE lane only. If you are about to add a card here because the page looks
// thin, add the benefit to the yml (where it is reviewed) or leave the page thin.
const memberBenefits = memberTier?.benefits ?? [];
const memberRevenue = memberTier?.revenue ?? '';

// Every FAQ that sold a Creator benefit is GONE rather than reworded, because rewording means hand-writing
// claims again one file away from the thing that just broke. Cut: the editorial-submissions answer and the
// weekly-shop-talk answer (both Creator), and the revenue-splits answer (the first-touch/last-touch program
// is Creator; a Member earns through invites and nothing else). Kept and reworded to the READER side: what
// the network is, and how member-only content works. Kept unchanged: comments, the invite lane, and the
// founding story.
const faqs = [
  ['What is the GBTI Network?', 'A professional publishing network for developers. Members read and discuss the work published across it, take part in a private community, and earn on the members they bring in. Publishing your own articles, products and prompts is the Content Creator tier.'],
  ['What does GBTI stand for?', 'God Bless The Internet; a phrase that expresses appreciation and goodwill toward the continued growth and enrichment of the internet.'],
  ['How is the network built?', "The public git repository is the database. Every article, product, prompt, and profile lives as a plain file in a public repo. There is no traditional CMS and no separate content database, and the static site is the published read-view. Membership status is derived from Stripe rather than a separate user database, and every lookup matches on your immutable GitHub id."],
  ['Do members earn for inviting people?', `Yes. A personal invite link earns a flat ${INVITE_PCT} lifetime commission when someone joins through it, for as long as they keep paying.`],
  ['Is all content public or private?', 'Both. Some work is published openly, and some is network-only. For network-only work, a stub with a short description appears on the public website, while the full content is readable by members inside the login-gated browser extension.'],
  ['Are comments on public-facing content also public?', 'By default, they are not, and can only be read inside the extension by other members. There is, however, the option to make a comment fully public.'],
  // The founding story is REUSED verbatim in substance (owner, 2026-08-15: it is true for this audience
  // too), because it is a fact about GBTI rather than a claim about the reader. The Codeable version's next
  // sentence complimented the audience ("the expertise at Codeable is well known and respected"). There is
  // no sourced equivalent here, so it is OMITTED and nothing is substituted for it. Inventing audience
  // flattery is what put a fabricated origin story live and into syndication on 2026-07-30.
  ['Why is my first year free?', `The GBTI Network was founded by members of the Codeable network seeking a place to discuss the nuances of product development. Your invite covers a full year at the ${TIER_LABEL} tier, with no card required, and nothing bills automatically. If you choose to stay, it is ${TIER_PRICE_LABEL} per ${BILLING_PERIOD}.`],
];

const year = new Date().getFullYear();
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Your first year on us"
  description="A private invitation: a full year at the Network Member tier, first year free with your coupon."
  noindex
  bare
>
  <div class="ci">

    <!-- ================= NAV ================= -->
    <div class="ci-nav">
      <div class="ci-nav-in">
        <a class="ci-brand" href="/" aria-label="GBTI Network home">
          <img src="/brand/logo/mark-green.png" alt="" width="30" height="30" class="mark-light" />
          <img src="/brand/logo/mark-mint.png" alt="" width="30" height="30" class="mark-dark" />
          <span>GBTI</span>
        </a>
        <nav class="ci-links" aria-label="Sections">
          <a href="#benefits">What you get</a>
          <a href="#faq">FAQ</a>
        </nav>
        <button type="button" class="ci-theme" data-ci-theme aria-label="Toggle dark mode">
          <svg class="ico-sun" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="15" height="15" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="4"/><path d="M12 2v2M12 20v2M4.9 4.9l1.4 1.4M17.7 17.7l1.4 1.4M2 12h2M20 12h2M4.9 19.1l1.4-1.4M17.7 6.3l1.4-1.4"/></svg>
          <svg class="ico-moon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="15" height="15" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M21 12.8A9 9 0 1 1 11.2 3a7 7 0 0 0 9.8 9.8Z"/></svg>
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ================= HERO ================= -->
    <div class="ci-hero">
      <div class="ci-hero-in">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Your invitation</p>
          <h1>Welcome to GBTI Network</h1>
          <p class="lead">GBTI is a professional publishing network for developers. Read the work published
            across it, join the conversation, and earn on the members you bring in. Your invite covers a full
            year at the {TIER_LABEL} tier, with no card required.</p>
          <div class="ci-cta-row">
            <a href="#claim" class="btn-primary">Claim your free year</a>
            <a href="#benefits" class="btn-ghost">What you get</a>
          </div>
          <!-- The ticks are the FIRST THREE YML BULLETS, not a hand-picked summary. A summary is prose, and
               prose is what put Creator benefits on a member page. -->
          <div class="ci-ticks">
            {memberBenefits.slice(0, 3).map((b) => (<span>&#10003; &nbsp;{b}</span>))}
          </div>
        </div>
        <div id="claim" class="ci-claim">
          <p class="eyebrow tcenter" style="margin-bottom:0">{TIER_LABEL}</p>
          <div class="ci-price">Year one free</div>
          <div class="ci-sub">then {TIER_PRICE_LABEL}/{BILLING_PERIOD} if you choose to stay</div>
          <div class="ci-rule"></div>
          <div class="ci-coupon-label">Coupon</div>
          <div class="ci-chip" data-coupon-chip>
            <input id="ci-coupon" type="text" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" placeholder="Enter your coupon code" aria-label="Coupon code" />
            <span class="applied" data-coupon-applied hidden>&#10003; applied</span>
          </div>
          <div class="signup-cta">
            <div class="cf-turnstile" data-sitekey={TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY} data-callback="gbtiTurnstileOk" data-expired-callback="gbtiTurnstileReset" data-error-callback="gbtiTurnstileFail" data-theme="auto"></div>
            <button id="signup-go" type="button" class="btn-primary btn-claim" disabled>Claim your free year</button>
            <p class="ci-ts-note" data-ts-note hidden>The human verification did not load, so the button stays
              disabled. If you use a content blocker, allow challenges.cloudflare.com and refresh this page.</p>
          </div>
          <p class="ci-fine">Sign in with GitHub. No card at any point during the free year, and nothing
            bills automatically.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>


    <!-- ================= BENEFITS ================= -->
    <section id="benefits" class="ci-sec">
      <p class="eyebrow">Why members join</p>
      <h2 style="max-width:20ch">What {TIER_LABEL} gives you</h2>
      <p class="sec-lead">{memberTier?.tagline}</p>
      <div class="grid3">
        {memberBenefits.map((b) => (
          <div class="card lift bcard">
            <div class="bod"><h3>{b}</h3></div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      {memberRevenue && (
        <div class="ci-invite-lane">
          <div class="ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="19" height="19" fill="none" stroke="var(--ci-green-ink)" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M4 4h16v16H4z"/><path d="M22 6l-10 7L2 6"/></svg></div>
          <p><strong>{memberRevenue}</strong></p>
        </div>
      )}
    </section>

    <!-- ================= FAQ ================= -->
    <section id="faq" class="ci-sec ci-faq">
      <p class="eyebrow tcenter">Questions and answers</p>
      <h2 class="tcenter">Network FAQ</h2>
      <div class="ci-faq-list">
        {faqs.map(([q, a]) => (
          <div class="ci-q card">
            <button type="button" data-faq aria-expanded="false">
              <span>{q}</span><span class="sign" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
            </button>
            <div class="ci-a" hidden>{a}</div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ================= FOOTER ================= -->
    <div class="ci-foot">
      <div class="ci-foot-in">
        <span class="ci-brand"><img src="/brand/logo/mark-green.png" alt="" width="26" height="26" class="mark-light" /><img src="/brand/logo/mark-mint.png" alt="" width="26" height="26" class="mark-dark" /><span class="god">GOD BLESS THE INTERNET</span></span>
        <span class="cr">&copy; {year} GBTI Network</span>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<script is:inline src="https://challenges.cloudflare.com/turnstile/v0/api.js" async defer></script>
<script define:vars={{ signupBase: SIGNUP_BASE, refCookie: REF_COOKIE, viaCookie: REF_VIA_COOKIE, sidCookie: TOUCH_SID_COOKIE, touchEnabled: TOUCH_CAPTURE_ENABLED }}>
  // The SOW-119 mechanics under the design skin: token -> locked "applied" chip; otherwise manual entry.
  // The CTA is the same Turnstile-gated /signup/start navigation as /membership/, plus the coupon param.
  (function () {
    function cookie(name) {
      var c = document.cookie.split('; ').find(function (x) { return x.indexOf(name + '=') === 0; });
      return c ? decodeURIComponent(c.split('=').slice(1).join('=')) : '';
    }
    var input = document.getElementById('ci-coupon');
    var chip = document.querySelector('[data-coupon-chip]');
    var applied = document.querySelector('[data-coupon-applied]');
    // A visible ?coupon=CODE prefills the chip (QA 2026-07-18: no secret token links). The field stays
    // editable; the applied badge shows while the value matches the shared code.
    var shared = (new URLSearchParams(location.search).get('coupon') || '').trim().toUpperCase();
    function syncApplied() {
      var match = shared && input && input.value.trim().toUpperCase() === shared;
      chip.classList.toggle('locked', Boolean(match));
      if (applied) applied.hidden = !match;
    }
    if (shared && /^[A-Z0-9]{3,32}$/.test(shared) && input) {
      input.value = shared;
      syncApplied();
      input.addEventListener('input', syncApplied);
    }

    var btn = document.getElementById('signup-go');
    var tsNote = document.querySelector('[data-ts-note]');
    window.gbtiTurnstileOk = function (token) {
      if (btn) { btn.disabled = false; btn.dataset.token = token; }
      if (tsNote) tsNote.hidden = true;
    };
    window.gbtiTurnstileReset = function () { if (btn) { btn.disabled = true; delete btn.dataset.token; } };
    // Widget error (network failure, blocked frame): reset the button and explain why it is disabled.
    window.gbtiTurnstileFail = function () {
      window.gbtiTurnstileReset();
      if (tsNote) tsNote.hidden = false;
      return true;
    };
    // Blocked script: api.js never arrives, no callback ever fires, the button would stay silently dead.
    setTimeout(function () {
      if (!window.turnstile && tsNote && btn && btn.disabled) tsNote.hidden = false;
    }, 8000);
    if (btn) btn.addEventListener('click', function () {
      var token = btn.dataset.token;
      if (!token) return;
      var u = new URL(signupBase + '/signup/start');
      u.searchParams.set('cf-turnstile-response', token);
      var code = input && input.value ? input.value.trim() : '';
      if (code) u.searchParams.set('coupon', code);
      var ref = cookie(refCookie); if (ref) u.searchParams.set('ref', ref);
      var via = cookie(viaCookie); if (via) u.searchParams.set('via', via);
      if (touchEnabled) { var sid = cookie(sidCookie); if (sid) u.searchParams.set('sid', sid); }
      window.location.href = u.toString();
    });

    // The design's theme toggle, wired to the site's html[data-theme] + the persisted gbti-theme key.
    document.querySelector('[data-ci-theme]')?.addEventListener('click', function () {
      var root = document.documentElement;
      var next = root.getAttribute('data-theme') === 'dark' ? 'light' : 'dark';
      root.setAttribute('data-theme', next);
      try { localStorage.setItem('gbti-theme', next); } catch (e) { /* no storage */ }
    });

    // FAQ accordion: one open at a time, the +/- sign mirrors state.
    var qs = Array.prototype.slice.call(document.querySelectorAll('[data-faq]'));
    qs.forEach(function (b) {
      b.addEventListener('click', function () {
        var a = b.nextElementSibling;
        var open = a && a.hidden === false;
        qs.forEach(function (o) {
          var oa = o.nextElementSibling;
          if (oa) oa.hidden = true;
          o.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');
          var s = o.querySelector('.sign'); if (s) s.textContent = '+';
        });
        if (!open && a) {
          a.hidden = false;
          b.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'true');
          var s2 = b.querySelector('.sign'); if (s2) s2.textContent = '−';
        }
      });
    });
  })();
</script>

<style>
  /* The design's surface palette mapped onto the site's html[data-theme] switch. Light is the default. */
  .ci {
    --ci-surface: #ffffff; --ci-hero: #fbfbfa; --ci-panel: #f5f4f2; --ci-sunk: #f5f4f2; --ci-chip: #ffffff;
    --ci-line: rgba(20,17,26,.10); --ci-line2: rgba(20,17,26,.2); --ci-navline: rgba(20,17,26,.08);
    --ci-fg: #1a1720; --ci-soft: #55505c; --ci-mute: #847f8d; --ci-faint: #a7a2ad;
    --ci-green: #178a50; --ci-green-ink: #1f9e5f; --ci-amber: #a9781c; --ci-pill: #ffffff; --ci-bg: #f2f0ee;
    background: var(--ci-bg); color: var(--ci-fg); min-height: 100vh;
  }
  :global(html[data-theme="dark"]) .ci {
    --ci-surface: #232029; --ci-hero: #232029; --ci-panel: #2a2731; --ci-sunk: #1d1a23; --ci-chip: #17151c;
    --ci-line: rgba(255,255,255,.09); --ci-line2: rgba(255,255,255,.16); --ci-navline: rgba(255,255,255,.07);
    --ci-fg: #f3f2f0; --ci-soft: #bdbac4; --ci-mute: #847f8d; --ci-faint: #5c5865;
    --ci-green: #5fd49a; --ci-amber: #f0c883; --ci-pill: #2a2731; --ci-bg: #17151c;
  }
  .ci .mark-dark { display: none; }
  :global(html[data-theme="dark"]) .ci .mark-light { display: none; }
  :global(html[data-theme="dark"]) .ci .mark-dark { display: inline; }
  .ci .ico-moon { display: none; }
  :global(html[data-theme="dark"]) .ci .ico-sun { display: none; }
  :global(html[data-theme="dark"]) .ci .ico-moon { display: inline; }

  .ci a { color: var(--ci-green); text-decoration: none; }
  .ci a:hover { color: var(--ci-green-ink); }
  .ci .eyebrow { font-family: var(--f-mono); font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .16em; color: var(--ci-green); margin: 0 0 14px; }
  .ci .tcenter { text-align: center; }
  .ci h2 { font-family: var(--f-display); font-weight: 700; font-size: clamp(30px, 4.4vw, 40px); line-height: 1.08; letter-spacing: -0.015em; color: var(--ci-fg); margin: 0 0 16px; }
  .ci .sec-lead { font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ci-soft); max-width: 66ch; margin: 0 0 44px; }

  .btn-primary { background: #1f9e5f; color: #fff; font-weight: 700; border-radius: 7px; border: 0; cursor: pointer; display: inline-block; font-size: 15px; padding: 15px 26px; box-shadow: 0 6px 20px rgba(31,158,95,.35); transition: transform .12s, box-shadow .2s; }
  .btn-primary:hover:not(:disabled) { color: #fff; transform: translateY(-1px); box-shadow: 0 10px 28px rgba(31,158,95,.45); }
  .btn-primary:disabled { opacity: .55; cursor: default; }
  .btn-ghost { border: 1px solid var(--ci-line2); color: var(--ci-fg); font-weight: 600; border-radius: 7px; font-size: 15px; padding: 14px 24px; }
  .btn-ghost:hover { color: var(--ci-fg); border-color: var(--ci-green); }
  /* The hero CTAs are anchors, and `.ci a` outranks `.btn-*` on specificity, so re-assert the button ink. */
  .ci a.btn-primary, .ci a.btn-primary:hover { color: #fff; }
  .ci a.btn-ghost, .ci a.btn-ghost:hover { color: var(--ci-fg); }
  .lift { transition: transform .15s, border-color .2s; }
  .lift:hover { transform: translateY(-3px); border-color: rgba(31,158,95,.45); }
  .card { background: var(--ci-panel); border: 1px solid var(--ci-line); border-radius: 7px; }

  /* nav */
  .ci-nav { position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 20; background: var(--ci-surface); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--ci-navline); }
  /* the sticky nav is ~63px tall; without this every anchor jump lands the section under the bar */
  .ci-sec, .ci-band, .ci-claim { scroll-margin-top: 78px; }
  .ci-nav-in { max-width: 1160px; margin: 0 auto; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 28px; padding: 14px 40px; }
  .ci-brand { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 11px; font-family: var(--f-display); font-weight: 700; font-size: 19px; color: var(--ci-fg) !important; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  .ci-links { display: flex; gap: 24px; font-size: 14px; margin-left: 8px; }
  .ci-links a { color: var(--ci-soft); }
  .ci-links a:hover { color: var(--ci-fg); }
  .ci-theme { margin-left: auto; width: 34px; height: 34px; border-radius: 50%; border: 1px solid var(--ci-line); background: var(--ci-pill); color: var(--ci-soft); cursor: pointer; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .ci-links { display: none; } }

  /* hero + claim card */
  .ci-hero { background: var(--ci-hero); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--ci-navline); }
  .ci-hero-in { max-width: 1160px; margin: 0 auto; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 400px; gap: 56px; padding: 72px 40px 76px; }
  @media (max-width: 960px) { .ci-hero-in { grid-template-columns: 1fr; padding: 48px 24px 56px; } }
  .ci-hero h1 { font-family: var(--f-display); font-weight: 700; font-size: clamp(40px, 6vw, 64px); line-height: 1.02; letter-spacing: -0.02em; color: var(--ci-fg); margin: 0 0 24px; text-wrap: balance; }
  .ci-hero .eyebrow { margin-bottom: 22px; }
  .ci-hero .lead { font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ci-soft); max-width: 46ch; margin: 0 0 34px; }
  .ci-cta-row { display: flex; gap: 13px; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .ci-ticks { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 26px; margin-top: 38px; font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--ci-mute); }

  .ci-claim { background: var(--ci-panel); border: 1px solid var(--ci-line); border-radius: 7px; padding: 30px 28px; align-self: start; }
  .ci-price { font-family: var(--f-display); font-weight: 700; font-size: 34px; color: var(--ci-fg); text-align: center; margin-top: 6px; }
  .ci-sub { text-align: center; color: var(--ci-mute); font-size: 13.5px; margin-top: 4px; }
  .ci-rule { height: 1px; background: var(--ci-line); margin: 24px 0; }
